        {
          "title": "Fisher-Informed Recalibration for Feedback-Based On-Policy Self-Distillation of LLMs",
          "title_zh": "面向 LLM 反馈式同策略自蒸馏的 Fisher 信息重校准",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.34009v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.34009",
          "summary": "FIRE is a dual-branch framework that stabilizes feedback-based on-policy self-distillation by replacing self-distillation with re-weighted on-policy SFT for correct responses and recalibrating the feedback-conditioned target for incorrect ones, using a token-level radius derived in part from a softmax Fisher trace. Experiments report substantially more stable self-distillation while maintaining strong downstream performance, particularly where standard feedback-conditioned distillation becomes unstable.",
