        {
          "title": "3D Point Tracking with State Space Models",
          "title_zh": "基于状态空间模型的三维点跟踪",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.34035v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.34035",
          "summary": "The method composes frozen dense optical flow and monocular metric-depth front-ends and learns only the residual depth with a compact Mamba-3 state space model conditioned on DINOv3 appearance features, targeting metric 3D point tracking on a single commodity GPU without poses. On the TAPVid-3D minival benchmark its best configuration attains the highest absolute metric accuracy among methods evaluated under identical conditions (mean metric Average Jaccard 0.256), and a companion analysis explains why several published trackers lose most of their accuracy under the same budget.",
