        {
          "title": "Faithful Activation Verbalization: Reducing Hallucinations in LLM Representation Interpretation",
          "title_zh": "忠实的激活言语化：减少 LLM 表示解释中的幻觉",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.34033v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.34033",
          "summary": "AVPO is a two-stage framework that first reconstructs source text from a hidden activation and then evaluates the reconstruction with a separate frozen question-answering model, yielding an inspectable intermediate readout, with the inverter optimized by DPO using rewards for semantic recoverability and lexical fidelity. Across six text families it improves gist- and detail-level information recovery over the strongest baseline by up to 17.1 and 9.3 percentage points, and an out-of-distribution case study shows it better recovers high-level semantics while fabricating fewer details.",
