        {
          "title": "PerceptFence: Content-Mediation Architecture and Deterministic Coverage for Screen-Share AI Assistants",
          "title_zh": "PerceptFence：屏幕共享 AI 助手的内容中介架构与确定性覆盖",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.34027v2",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.34027",
          "summary": "PerceptFence is a content-layer mediation architecture between capture, memory, and model responses for live screen-share assistants, evaluated with a deterministic synthetic-fixture scaffold rather than live capture. On 480 synthetic developer-support screens rendered, degraded, and read by OCR, it neutralizes 889 of 968 OCR-surviving secrets and PII values (0.918; Wilson 95% 0.899-0.934) against 0.581 for Presidio and 0.179 for gitleaks, and 0.974 on held-out screen types, at a measured cost of 0.763 task-token retention.",
