          "title": "T-SNN: Temporal Simplicial Neural Network for EEG Decoding",
          "title_zh": "T-SNN：用于脑电解码的时间单纯形神经网络",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.34002v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.34002",
          "summary": "T-SNN represents EEG recordings as sequences of evolving simplicial complexes and combines simplicial convolutions with recurrent updates to jointly learn higher-order interactions among brain regions and their temporal evolution. On the seven-class SEED-VII emotion recognition task it outperforms convolutional, recurrent, graph-based, and Transformer methods in both trial-wise and cross-subject evaluations, and incorporating eye-movement features yields further gains.",
