          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.34004",
          "summary": "RICE-Alpha is a point-in-time stock-scoring framework that separates a history-aware multi-view Base Alpha from a reliability-calibrated residual correction derived from historical event continuation, using a Multi-Tier Memory Layer and typed event graphs that preserve issuer-specific chronology under point-in-time constraints. On daily Nasdaq-100 and Hang Seng panels from 2024 to 2026 it reports the strongest results among evaluated LLM-based agents on four predictive and four portfolio metrics, with ICIR more than double the strongest baseline and net Sharpe ratios of 1.656 and 1.725 in the U.S. and Hong Kong.",
